From 0db5d6efc739bf3657f8729a7e7c50728f45f600 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:23:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] volumes: resolve missing Pod UID before selecting CSI
 disks

Kata remote CreateVM can send only the Pod name and namespace. When its
annotations omit a UID, the existing scan includes direct volumes from
other Pods on the worker.

Resolve the UID through the existing PeerPod Kubernetes client once a CSI
entry is found, and fail selection if the lookup cannot identify the Pod.
Keep the existing annotation/CRI-O paths and metadata format. Reuse the
volume fixtures and cover the missing-UID path through a local API server.

Signed-off-by: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Co-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
